## What a `type: codebase` instance is

**One memorial per registered code repository**, declaring frontmatter that connects the repo to the corpus's introspection substrate.  The memorial itself is light-weight; the detail-level structure (which function lives where, who calls what, namespace requires, dispatch tables) lives ONLY in a per-repo xref index built by code-introspection tooling (e.g., `clj-xref` for Clojure repos).

There is **no parallel hierarchy of namespace / function / var memorials** — a codebase is reified at a single granularity (the repo), and finer-grained navigation goes through the introspection substrate.

Codebase is a subtype of [`artifact`](artifact.md), and uses [`code-meta-type`](code-meta-type.md) composition (instead of the default markdown-meta-type) for detail-level navigation.

